---
layout: layouts/page.njk
eyebrow: Astronomy
title: Astronomy
description: Astrophotography and research on the black hole X-ray binary V4641 Sagittarii.
---
{% from "partials/writings-list.njk" import writingsList %}

<section id="gallery" data-nav-section="/astronomy/">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2>Gallery</h2>
      <div class="gallery-grid">
        {% for item in gallery %}
          <figure class="gallery-item">
            <div class="placeholder-block" style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;">
              <span>{{ item.filename }} — {{ item.dimensions }}</span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>{{ item.title }}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="research" data-nav-section="/astronomy/">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2>Research</h2>
      <p class="eyebrow">STARS Summer Research Program, 2023 — Prof. Charles Bailyn</p>
      <p>
        Analysed twenty years of optical and infrared data from the black hole
        X-ray binary V4641 Sagittarii. Used Python, Excel, Siril, and SAOImage
        for stellar data analysis; NumPy, AstroPy, and SciPy for timelines and
        optical data initialisation — alignment, dithering, and differential
        aperture photometry.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="writings" data-nav-section="/astronomy/">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2>Writings</h2>
      {{ writingsList(collections.writings | byTag("astronomy") | reverse, "Notes on astrophotography and observing — coming soon.") }}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
